1 REM
2 REM THE RUGG/FELDMAN BENCHMARKS, BM1-BM8.
3 REM PUBLISHED IN KILOBAUD JUNE 1977; BM8 IS JOHN COLL'S,
4 REM PERSONAL COMPUTER WORLD FEBRUARY 1978.
5 REM
6 REM THE LISTINGS ARE THE PUBLISHED ONES. THE ONLY CHANGE
7 REM IS THAT "IF K<1000 THEN 500" IS WRITTEN "THEN GOTO",
8 REM WHICH THIS BASIC REQUIRES AND WHICH COSTS NOTHING.
9 REM
10 MODE 0
20 POKE $FF24,0
30 DIM T(8)
35 N=1
36 R=10
40 DIM M(5)
50 PRINT "RUGG/FELDMAN BM1-BM8 -- 10 RUNS EACH, AVERAGED"
60 PRINT
100 PRINT "BM1 EMPTY FOR LOOP  ";:GOSUB 9000
104 FOR P=1 TO R
110 FOR K=1 TO 1000
120 NEXT K
125 NEXT P
130 GOSUB 9100
200 PRINT "BM2 LOOP AND COUNT  ";:GOSUB 9000
204 FOR P=1 TO R
210 K=0
220 K=K+1
230 IF K<1000 THEN GOTO 220
235 NEXT P
240 GOSUB 9100
300 PRINT "BM3 ...AND DIVIDE   ";:GOSUB 9000
304 FOR P=1 TO R
310 K=0
320 K=K+1
330 A=K/K*K+K-K
340 IF K<1000 THEN GOTO 320
345 NEXT P
350 GOSUB 9100
400 PRINT "BM4 ...ON CONSTANTS ";:GOSUB 9000
404 FOR P=1 TO R
410 K=0
420 K=K+1
430 A=K/2*3+4-5
440 IF K<1000 THEN GOTO 420
445 NEXT P
450 GOSUB 9100
500 PRINT "BM5 ...AND A GOSUB  ";:GOSUB 9000
504 FOR P=1 TO R
510 K=0
520 K=K+1
530 A=K/2*3+4-5
540 GOSUB 8000
550 IF K<1000 THEN GOTO 520
555 NEXT P
560 GOSUB 9100
600 PRINT "BM6 ...AND A LOOP   ";:GOSUB 9000
604 FOR P=1 TO R
610 K=0
620 K=K+1
630 A=K/2*3+4-5
640 GOSUB 8000
650 FOR L=1 TO 5
660 NEXT L
670 IF K<1000 THEN GOTO 620
675 NEXT P
680 GOSUB 9100
700 PRINT "BM7 ...AND AN ARRAY ";:GOSUB 9000
704 FOR P=1 TO R
710 K=0
720 K=K+1
730 A=K/2*3+4-5
740 GOSUB 8000
750 FOR L=1 TO 5
760 M(L)=A
770 NEXT L
780 IF K<1000 THEN GOTO 720
785 NEXT P
790 GOSUB 9100
800 PRINT "BM8 TRANSCENDENTALS ";:GOSUB 9000
804 FOR P=1 TO R
810 K=0
820 K=K+1
830 A=K^2
840 B=LOG(K)
850 C=SIN(K)
860 IF K<100 THEN GOTO 820
865 NEXT P
870 GOSUB 9100
880 GOTO 1000
7999 REM THE EMPTY SUBROUTINE BM5 ONWARDS CALLS
8000 RETURN
8999 REM
9000 REM START: THE FRAME COUNTER IS THE CLOCK. 24 BITS AT
9001 REM 59.97 HZ, AND READING IT COSTS THREE PEEKS -- WHICH
9002 REM IS WHY THE "RUNNING" TEXT IS PRINTED BEFORE THIS.
9003 REM
9010 S=PEEK($FF2D)
9012 U=PEEK($FF2E)
9020 RETURN
9100 E=PEEK($FF2D)
9102 F=PEEK($FF2E)
9104 D=E-S
9106 G=F-U
9108 IF D<0 THEN D=D+256
9109 IF E<S THEN G=G-1
9110 IF G<0 THEN G=G+256
9111 T(N)=(D+G*256)/59.97/R
9120 PRINT T(N);" S"
9130 N=N+1
9140 RETURN
999 REM
1000 REM THE REPORT. EVERY OTHER MACHINE'S FIGURES ARE THE
1001 REM PUBLISHED ONES, ALL FROM THE ONE TABLE SO THEY ARE
1002 REM COMPARABLE WITH EACH OTHER. IBM PC, MSX, AMSTRAD
1003 REM CPC AND TRS-80 ARE NOT IN IT AND ARE LEFT OUT
1004 REM RATHER THAN MIXED IN FROM SOMEWHERE ELSE.
1005 REM
1010 CLS
1020 PRINT "RUGG/FELDMAN BM1-BM8, SECONDS. LOWER IS BETTER."
1030 PRINT
1040 PRINT "MACHINE          BM1   BM2   BM3   BM4   BM5   BM6   BM7   BM8"
1050 PRINT "--------------------------------------------------------------"
1060 PRINT "COOL8 8.375MHZ";
1070 FOR I=1 TO 8
1072 PRINT " ";
1074 GOSUB 9200
1076 NEXT I
1080 PRINT
1090 PRINT "COOL8 AT 1MHZ ";
1100 FOR I=1 TO 8
1102 PRINT " ";
1104 V=T(I)*8.375
1106 GOSUB 9300
1108 NEXT I
1110 PRINT
1120 PRINT "BBC MICRO     ";
1122 GOSUB 1400
1124 PRINT "LUXOR ABC 80  ";
1126 GOSUB 1400
1128 PRINT "APPLE II      ";
1130 GOSUB 1400
1132 PRINT "COMMODORE 64  ";
1134 GOSUB 1400
1136 PRINT "VIC-20        ";
1138 GOSUB 1400
